! LOAD TRANSIT AND SET, both radices, and decimal MULTIPLY, DIVIDE and
! MULTIPLY AND ADD, which are LTRS's action -- G2.3, built 2026-11-16.
!
! Expected values HAND-DERIVED from the Reference Manual 22-6530-2, read in
! the page images; none from a run.
!   printed p.67 (PDF 70), LTRS: "The transit register (location 15), the
!     left zeros counter, and the all-ones counter are cleared.  A four-bit
!     sign byte, in which the leftmost bit is set to the sign of the
!     addressed storage operand as modified by the negative sign modifier,
!     is placed in the four low-order bits of the transit register.  The
!     remaining three bits of this sign byte are zero.  The numeric part of
!     the addressed operand is positioned immediately to the left of this
!     sign byte in the transit register.  The effective offset specified by
!     the instruction is placed in the all-ones counter (bits 44-50 of
!     location 7).  The two high-order bits of the left zeros counter (bits
!     17-18 of location 7) are set to ones."
!   printed p.68 (PDF 71): "either the binary-transit or decimal-transit
!     indicator is turned on, depending on the value of the radix
!     modifier"; PF "if the numeric part of the field loaded contains more
!     than 60 significant bits ... the transit register is loaded up to its
!     left end.  Higher-order bits are lost"; TF/UF/VF and MOP "as in ADD";
!     RLZ/RZ/RGZ/RN "according to the contents of the transit register";
!     the table MULTIPLY 00, DIVIDE 01, MULTIPLY AND ADD 10, LOAD TRANSIT
!     AND SET 11.  MULTIPLY, same page: "If decimal is specified, this
!     operation has the same action as LOAD TRANSIT AND SET, except that
!     the two high-order bits of the left zeros counter are set to zeros."
!   printed p.69 (PDF 72), *+: "... set to 10"; printed p.70 (PDF 73),
!     DIVIDE: "... set to 01".
!   printed p.21 (PDF 24): the second half's I field modifies bits 35-50,
!     "bit position 3 of the index word is aligned with bit position 35".
!
! READINGS CHOSEN (no page decides them):
!  * A DECIMAL operand's numeric part goes into the transit register as
!    FOUR-BIT digits, each byte's zone dropped -- "Radix.  This modifier
!    operates as in ADD" (p.68), and ADD's decimal operand is "converted
!    to a four-bit byte for processing" (p.58).  The other reading, the
!    bytes as they stand, would make T6 (16)F1F2F3F40.
!  * The full seven-bit effective offset goes to the all-ones counter, in
!    decimal too (p.60's "two low-order bits ... ignored" is ADD's).  W6
!    uses offset 12, where the two readings agree; open.
!  * Decimal result indicators as the decimal arms set them (RN is the
!    sign, so a negative zero would set it), binary as the binary arms
!    (the same rule since 2026-11-16: printed p.47, RN "negative whether
!    zero or not").
!
! Word 7 here is the model's: IBM 17-23 the left zeros count, 44-50 the
! all-ones count, so W = (lzc << 40) | (aoc << 13).  Indicator masks: BTR
! (16)1000000, DTR 800000, PF 10000000000, TF 10000000, VF 4000000, RLZ
! 80, RZ 40, RGZ 20, RN 10.  Sign byte 8 bits wide: the sign is its bit 3
! from the right, the flags T U V its bits 2-0 (fieldToSM's reading).
!
!  1 LTRS(BU,24,8) 123456, offset 37: T1 1234560, W1 lzc 1100000 aoc 37 =
!    000060000004A000, I1 BTR RGZ.
!  2 LTRS(B,32,8) 00ABCD 08 (sign byte 08: minus, no flags), offset 0:
!    T2 ABCD8, W2 0000600000000000, I2 BTR RLZ RN.
!  3 LTRS(B,16,8) 77 05 (plus, flags T and V): T3 770 (the flags are NOT
!    loaded: "the remaining three bits ... are zero"), I3 BTR TF VF RGZ.
!  4 LTRS(BU,64,8) F000000000000001: 64 significant bits > 60, PF; TR
!    keeps the low 60, T4 10, I4 BTR PF RGZ.
!  5 LTRS(BU,8,8) offset 5 indexed by $3 = 0.96 (index bit 18 is the
!    offset's units bit: +3): W5 lzc 1100000 aoc 8 = 0000600000010000.
!  6 LTRS(DU,32,8) F1 F2 F3 F4, offset 12: T6 12340, W6 0000600000018000,
!    I6 DTR RGZ.
!  7 *(D,24,4) 12345 8 (minus), offset 20: lzc 00, T7 123458,
!    W7 0000000000028000, I7 DTR RLZ RN -- not OP.
!  8 /(DU,16,8) 09 07, offset 4: lzc 01, T8 970, W8 0000200000008000,
!    I8 DTR RGZ.
!  9 *+(DU,8,8) F0, offset 0: lzc 10, T9 0, W9 0000400000000000, I9 DTR RZ.
! 10 LTRS(DU,64,4) 1000000000000002: sixteen digits, 61 significant bits,
!    PF; T10 20, I10 DTR PF RGZ.
! ACC: the accumulator, loaded (16)0123456789ABCDEF at offset 0 first, is
!    "not affected" by any of the ten (LTRS's page is silent; LFT's p.69
!    says it of LOAD FACTOR, and the decimal * page's programming note
!    has the factors "available in the accumulator and the transit
!    register"): $L 0, $R 0123456789ABCDEF.
!
! 11 L(BU,64),$TR right after an LTRS: R11 (16)1234560 (added after the
!    review; the I-box waits on E-box registers 7-15, StretchIBox's
!    eboxRegister, but a VFL fetch goes through the E-box itself).
!
! OBSERVED 2026-11-16: all 27 checks of cases 1-10 pass as hand-derived,
! first run.
!
! TIMING RE-PINNED 2026-11-16, 974 -> 1214 clocks, every value check
! unchanged: LTRS is now charged its measured Perf. Char. Vol. 2 page, PDF
! 123 -- 44 clocks binary (13.20 us), 66 decimal (19.81), 82 decimal above
! 48 bits (24.60) -- and decimal *, *+ and / that page's decimal figure,
! CHOSEN because their own pages (PDF 133-135) print binary rows only
! (StretchTiming.bsv).  Before: a MODEL PIN (CYCLES 974; 926 before case
! 11 was added), Table 3's row, 16 + 2 x/y clocks.  In the ten cases above each LTRS is followed
! by I-box transmits that hide the E-box's time -- with the old generic
! charge the deck counted the same 684 clocks then -- so eight LTRS are run
! back to back at the end, where the E-box is the critical path.
!
! INJECTIONS, measured 2026-11-16, each reverted from a saved copy (cmp):
!  A the left-zeros bits always 11 (lzHigh's case on LTRS's own code):
!    W7, W8, W9 fail -- (16)600000028000, 600000008000, 600000000000.
!  B a decimal operand's bytes loaded as they stand (no decCompact): T6
!    (16)F1F2F3F40, T8 9070, T9 F00 and I9 (RGZ for RZ) fail.
!  D LTRS charged the generic 8 + 2 x/y: only CYCLES fails, 870 for 926
!    (seven of the eight back-to-back LTRS, 8 clocks each; the first
!    overlaps the transmits before it).  Measured BEFORE case 11 was added;
!    not re-measured at 974 or at 1214.
!  E (at 1214, 2026-11-16, in a scratch copy of the tree) binary LFT/LTRS
!    charged 36 for PDF 123's 44: only CYCLES fails, 1143 for 1214, 71
!    fewer.  Every other check passes.
!
        SLC, 1000.0
START   L(BU,64), ACCV
        LVI, $3, 0.96
        Z, $IND
        LTRS(BU,24,8), DA, 37
        TI, 1, $TR, T1
        TI, 1, 7.0, W1
        TI, 1, $IND, I1
        Z, $IND
        LTRS(B,32,8), DB, 0
        TI, 1, $TR, T2
        TI, 1, 7.0, W2
        TI, 1, $IND, I2
        Z, $IND
        LTRS(B,16,8), DC
        TI, 1, $TR, T3
        TI, 1, $IND, I3
        Z, $IND
        LTRS(BU,64,8), DPF
        TI, 1, $TR, T4
        TI, 1, $IND, I4
        Z, $IND
        LTRS(BU,8,8), DA, 5($3)
        TI, 1, 7.0, W5
        Z, $IND
        LTRS(DU,32,8), DE, 12
        TI, 1, $TR, T6
        TI, 1, 7.0, W6
        TI, 1, $IND, I6
        Z, $IND
        *(D,24,4), DF, 20
        TI, 1, $TR, T7
        TI, 1, 7.0, W7
        TI, 1, $IND, I7
        Z, $IND
        /(DU,16,8), DG, 4
        TI, 1, $TR, T8
        TI, 1, 7.0, W8
        TI, 1, $IND, I8
        Z, $IND
        *+(DU,8,8), DH
        TI, 1, $TR, T9
        TI, 1, 7.0, W9
        TI, 1, $IND, I9
        Z, $IND
        LTRS(DU,64,4), DPD
        TI, 1, $TR, T10
        TI, 1, $IND, I10
        TI, 2, $L, ACC
! 11: a VFL fetch of $TR straight after an LTRS, no transmit between: the
! load must see the new transit register.  LTRS(BU,24,8) DA gives
! (16)1234560 (case 1), so L(BU,64),$TR leaves $R (16)1234560.
        LTRS(BU,24,8), DA
        L(BU,64), $TR
        TI, 1, $R, R11
! TIMING: eight LTRS back to back, so the E-box is the critical path (above,
! each LTRS is followed by I-box transmits that hide its time).
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
        LTRS(BU,64,8), ACCV
HALT    BEW, $
        SLC, 1100.0
ACCV    DD(BU,64), (16)0123456789ABCDEF
DA      DD(BU,24), (16)123456
        DD(BU,40), 0
DB      DD(BU,32), (16)00ABCD08
        DD(BU,32), 0
DC      DD(BU,16), (16)7705
        DD(BU,48), 0
DPF     DD(BU,64), (16)F000000000000001
DE      DD(BU,32), (16)F1F2F3F4
        DD(BU,32), 0
DF      DD(BU,24), (16)123458
        DD(BU,40), 0
DG      DD(BU,16), (16)0907
        DD(BU,48), 0
DH      DD(BU,8), (16)F0
        DD(BU,56), 0
DPD     DD(BU,64), (16)1000000000000002
        SLC, 1200.0
T1      DD(BU,64), 0
W1      DD(BU,64), 0
I1      DD(BU,64), 0
T2      DD(BU,64), 0
W2      DD(BU,64), 0
I2      DD(BU,64), 0
T3      DD(BU,64), 0
I3      DD(BU,64), 0
T4      DD(BU,64), 0
I4      DD(BU,64), 0
W5      DD(BU,64), 0
T6      DD(BU,64), 0
W6      DD(BU,64), 0
I6      DD(BU,64), 0
T7      DD(BU,64), 0
W7      DD(BU,64), 0
I7      DD(BU,64), 0
T8      DD(BU,64), 0
W8      DD(BU,64), 0
I8      DD(BU,64), 0
T9      DD(BU,64), 0
W9      DD(BU,64), 0
I9      DD(BU,64), 0
T10     DD(BU,64), 0
I10     DD(BU,64), 0
ACC     DD(BU,64), 0
        DD(BU,64), 0
R11     DD(BU,64), 0
        END, START
